# Trivy ignore list. Each entry: reason, package, date, follow-up.
# Only advisories that cannot be fixed by a dependency bump belong here.
# CI scans with --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed, so moderate and
# upstream-unfixed advisories are not reported today; they are recorded here
# so an accepted risk stays accepted if the severity gate is widened.
# Full triage: docs/progress-report.md ("Dependency audit").

# react-router 6.x (runtime, moderate). Fix requires the react-router v7
# major migration; low exposure in this SPA. Added 2026-10-04.
# Follow-up: migrate to react-router v7.
# Trivy reports them by CVE id (fixed in 7.18.0); GHSA aliases kept too.
CVE-2026-53666
CVE-2026-53669
GHSA-wrjc-x8rr-h8h6
GHSA-337j-9hxr-rhxg

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp (moderate, no upstream fix: package is
# deprecated). The backend never imports openpgp; govulncheck confirms the
# symbol is unreachable. Not currently reported by Trivy. Added 2026-10-04.
# Follow-up: drop when x/crypto removes openpgp or an advisory fix ships.
GO-2026-5932
